[0m[32m
[0m[32mWe've seen this work in places like North Dakota, which has had a state-owned bank for over a century. It's helped keep capital in rural communities and supported agricultural businesses that might struggle to get financing from big national banks. Public banks could also reinvest profits back into the community rather than extracting wealth as dividends.
