[0m[32mThere's also the equity dimension—private banks have historically engaged in redlining and discriminatory lending practices. A publicly-controlled bank with democratic oversight would have mechanisms to ensure equitable access to credit across different neighborhoods and demographics. And with lower overhead from not needing to generate shareholder returns, they could offer better rates to borrowers and savers.
