[0m[33m
[0m[32mI understand the impulse for retribution, but I'd respectfully push back on this. The evidence suggests capital punishment doesn't effectively deter crime compared to long sentences, and we know the system makes irreversible errors—innocent people have been exonerated from death row. Beyond that, I think we should ask whether a just society should mimic the violence it condemns. Life sentences protect public safety while allowing for correction if new evidence emerges. Countries without capital punishment have lower murder rates than the US, and most wealthy democracies have abolished it. I'd rather invest those resources in crime prevention, victim support, and rehabilitation programs that actually reduce harm to communities.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
[0m[33m
