[0m[33m
[0m[32mAbsolutely, I think this is a critical issue we need to address. Right now, Americans pay dramatically more for the same medications than patients in other developed countries. When we allow Medicare to directly negotiate drug prices with pharmaceutical companies, we're not just saving money—we're affirming that healthcare is a right, not a luxury good. Other countries do this successfully all the time. We could redirect those savings into preventive care, mental health services, and reaching underserved communities. The pharmaceutical industry argues innovation would suffer, but they still invest heavily in R&D in countries with price negotiations. This is about prioritizing people's health and financial security over corporate profit margins.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
