[0m[32mI absolutely support that idea. AI literacy should be a foundational skill for all students, not just a privilege for those in wealthy districts or specialized programs. When we make it mandatory from elementary school onward, we're ensuring equitable access to understanding technology that will shape their futures and our society.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mThis is about collective welfare and social equality. Students from lower-income communities often have the least exposure to computer science and emerging technologies, yet they're the ones most likely to face disruption in the job market. By making AI education mandatory and government-funded across all schools, we level the playing field.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mBeyond economics, there's a crucial democratic component. Citizens need to understand how AI algorithms affect their lives—from hiring decisions to loan approvals to criminal justice systems. An informed public can better advocate for responsible AI development and hold corporations and governments accountable for algorithmic bias and discrimination. This is essential for protecting workers' rights and ensuring technology serves our communities rather than exploiting them.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
