[0m[32mI completely agree. This is a fundamental issue of equality and fairness. Same-sex couples are just as capable of being loving, nurturing parents as heterosexual couples—decades of research consistently shows this. When we deny adoption rights based on sexual orientation, we're not protecting children; we're actually harming them by keeping them in the foster care system longer, separated from families that desperately want to care for them.
[0m[32m
[0m[32mBeyond the moral imperative, there's a practical angle too. We have hundreds of thousands of children in foster care waiting for permanent families. Expanding adoption rights to same-sex couples means more loving homes for vulnerable children. That's what should matter—whether people can provide a safe, stable environment filled with love and support.
