[0m[32mI think that's a really important policy to consider. Student debt has become a massive burden that's holding back an entire generation—people are delaying homeownership, starting families, and launching small businesses because they're crushed by loan payments. When we forgive student debt, we're investing in economic mobility and reducing inequality. The benefits ripple through the economy: people can spend money locally, start businesses, and contribute more fully to society. Plus, we subsidize loans for wealthy people through tax breaks all the time, so prioritizing education access for working and middle-class people is just about fairness. It also acknowledges that our higher education system has been broken—costs have skyrocketed while wages haven't kept pace. We need systemic change, and debt forgiveness is a crucial part of that.<|eot_id|>[0m[33m<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
